{
  "version": 1,
  "nav_cycle": null,
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Random Encounters",
    "note": "2-6 aircraft enter a ring 40-45 NM out at once, all at FL200, at 260-300 KT, each on a straight track through its own point within 8 NM of the center to where that line leaves the airspace: their tracks cross near the center, so encounters of every angle develop minutes after entry. The ENTRY spawn region draws them; its route rule gives each its track. Every aircraft is an agent. Its actions - a heading and a speed clearance, and resuming own navigation - let a policy fly a resolution and hand the aircraft back to its route; with no clearance given, the aircraft fly their routes."
  },
